000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. SORTUG.
000300* SORT USING and GIVING: the sort's input read from one file and
000400* its output written to another, by code the compiler writes
000500* rather than the program. Two keys, one descending on a DISPLAY
000600* number (ZD), one ascending on characters (CH). Expected output
000700* recorded from IBM ANS COBOL on TK5.
000800 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
000900 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001000 FILE-CONTROL.
001100     SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE.
001200     SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-OUTFILE.
001300     SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-SORTWK01.
001400 DATA DIVISION.
001500 FILE SECTION.
001600 FD  IN-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
001700 01  IN-REC  PIC X(80).
001800 FD  OUT-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
001900 01  OUT-REC PIC X(80).
002000 SD  SORT-FILE.
002100 01  S-REC.
002200     05  S-NAME   PIC X(10).
002300     05  S-DEPT   PIC 99.
002400     05  S-REST   PIC X(68).
002500 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002600 01  EOF PIC X VALUE 'N'.
002700 01  SR  PIC S9(4).
002800 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002900 MAIN-PARA.
003000     SORT SORT-FILE DESCENDING KEY S-DEPT ASCENDING KEY S-NAME
003100         USING IN-FILE GIVING OUT-FILE.
003200     MOVE SORT-RETURN TO SR.
003300     DISPLAY 'SORT-RETURN ' SR.
003400     OPEN INPUT OUT-FILE.
003500     READ OUT-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF.
003600     PERFORM SHOW-ONE UNTIL EOF = 'Y'.
003700     CLOSE OUT-FILE.
003800     DISPLAY 'END OF OUT-FILE'.
003900     STOP RUN.
004000 SHOW-ONE.
004100     DISPLAY OUT-REC.
004200     READ OUT-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF.
